{TOOL} — record contract (the verb set IS the role boundary)
verbs: register, opinion, petition-rule, halt, certify, friction, render, help
  register: FIRST ACTION at the sitting: register --run <runDir> --seat-id <SEAT_ID from your prompt>
  opinion: a ruling as an OPINION: --gap-id R3-2 --disposition carried|closed|... --principle "..." --tension "correctness vs economy" --review-flag "why a human should look" [--file rationale]
  petition-rule: rule on a petition: --petitioner <seatId> --class <class> --as granted|denied --file <opinion> (a halt is its own verb)
  halt: the safety boundary: --file <written opinion — capture relays it like a FAIL, never smoothed>
  certify: the run-end certification statement ("what I would want a human to re-examine"): --file <statement>
  friction: attributed friction (the bench seats had no event path before — the abort-surviving copy): --text|--file
  render: read-only projection refresh (any seat may invoke)

